Holding a volume key now keeps stepping

If you map long press to Volume up or Volume down, holding the key walks the volume the way the built-in keys do, instead of moving it one step. It buzzes once at the start, not on every step, and stops the moment you let go.

Everything else still fires once per hold: repeating a toggle or an app launch would be wrong, and a repeat on e-ink would redraw the screen each time.
